WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.101
Synthetic review file: Northstar’s cost-of-sales line already includes depreciation of 30.

00:00:06.341 --> 00:00:13.616
A draft spreadsheet adds back that 30 once, then adds it again because the cash-flow statement also lists depreciation.

00:00:13.856 --> 00:00:16.587
The second entry duplicates the same expense.

00:00:16.827 --> 00:00:20.731
Trace a number to its source instead of counting every place it appears.

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.405
A new machine costs 90 in cash.

00:00:23.645 --> 00:00:27.186
That purchase is not depreciation of 90 for this quarter.

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:36.130
Depreciation allocates an asset’s cost over its useful life; amortization typically allocates the cost of a finite-lived intangible.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.191
Adding those expenses back does not remove the need to buy or replace assets.

00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:46.660
Use income-tax expense recorded in the earnings figure, not a cash-tax payment.

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.572
In a signed bridge, a tax benefit of 5 is −5, not +5.

00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:56.100
Ordinary payroll and property taxes remain operating expenses.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.199
Loan principal is also not interest expense.

00:00:59.889 --> 00:01:15.121
Original check: net income −10, interest expense 8, income-tax benefit 5, depreciation 12 and amortization 3 produces EBITDA = −10 + 8 − 5 + 12 + 3 = 8.

00:01:15.361 --> 00:01:20.161
If an analyst turns the benefit into +5, the answer is overstated by 10.

00:01:20.851 --> 00:01:29.427
Extra proposed add-backs for restructuring, stock compensation or routine software subscriptions are not part of the basic acronym.

00:01:29.667 --> 00:01:36.323
They require separate scrutiny and a different measure label; a new label alone does not make an adjustment appropriate.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:38.101
Now it's your turn.

00:01:38.341 --> 00:01:44.954
The draft adds a recurring software subscription of 6 to Northstar’s standard EBITDA of 180.

00:01:45.194 --> 00:01:46.133
What do you do?

00:01:46.373 --> 00:01:49.487
